{"task_id": "HumanEval/14", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\n\ndef all_prefixes(string: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a string, return a list of all its prefixes, ordered from the shortest to the longest.\n\n    For example:\n    all_prefixes('abc') should return ['a', 'ab', 'abc']\n    all_prefixes('') should return []\n    all_prefixes('x') should return ['x']\n    \"\"\"\n    prefixes: List[str] = []\n    # Iterate from 1 up to the length of the string (inclusive)\n    # The slice string[0:i] will give prefixes of increasing length\n    for i in range(1, len(string) + 1):\n        prefixes.append(string[0:i])\n    return prefixes\n```"}
