{"task_id": "HumanEval/49", "solution": "```python\ndef modp(n: int, p: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates 2^n modulo p.\n\n    Args:\n        n: The exponent (non-negative integer).\n        p: The modulus (positive integer).\n\n    Returns:\n        An integer representing (2**n) % p.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If p is not a positive integer or n is not a non-negative integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(p, int) or p <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Modulus 'p' must be a positive integer.\")\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Exponent 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    return pow(2, n, p)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/50", "solution": "```python\ndef decode_shift(s: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    takes as input string encoded with encode_shift function. Returns decoded string.\n    \"\"\"\n    decoded_chars = []\n    for ch in s:\n        # The encode_shift function maps all input characters to lowercase letters 'a' through 'z'.\n        # Therefore, we only need to consider lowercase letters for decoding.\n        \n        # Calculate the 0-based index of the current character relative to 'a'.\n        current_index = ord(ch) - ord('a')\n        \n        # Reverse the shift of 5.\n        # To handle potential negative results from (current_index - 5),\n        # we add 26 before taking the modulo, ensuring the result is always positive and within 0-25.\n        original_index = (current_index - 5 + 26) % 26\n        \n        # Convert the 0-based index back to a character.\n        decoded_chars.append(chr(original_index + ord('a')))\n        \n    return \"\".join(decoded_chars)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/51", "solution": "```python\ndef remove_vowels(text: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Removes all occurrences of vowels (case-insensitive) from the input string.\n    Preserves all other characters in their original order and casing.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Define a set for efficient O(1) average time vowel lookup\n    vowels_set = {'a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u'}\n\n    # Initialize an empty list to store characters that are not vowels\n    result_chars = []\n\n    # Iterate through each character in the input string\n    for char in text:\n        # Convert the character to lowercase for case-insensitive comparison\n        char_lower = char.lower()\n\n        # Check if the lowercase character is NOT in the vowels set\n        if char_lower not in vowels_set:\n            # If it's not a vowel, add the ORIGINAL character to our list\n            result_chars.append(char)\n\n    # Join all collected non-vowel characters into a single string\n    return \"\".join(result_chars)\n```"}
